Z||000000||MooCow||04-09-2001||09:22 PM||||What grit sand paper do I use for repinting my dash and the vents?  Also can I use the same yellow I used on my car on the vents and put clear on them or not?  I am painting the dash black and the vents will be yellow like my car.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Taijiguy||04-09-2001||10:08 PM||||I don't think it would do any good to sand the dash, since you aren't going to get into the grain anyway. I would just clean it really well as has been described in other dash coloring threads. I think the only thing I would do different from what I've read is I would use Prep-sol for my last wipe down. And yeah, there's no reason you couldn't paint the vents. Use a detail gu to spray them, should work out OK.<BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rex||04-09-2001||10:13 PM||||Ken, I would guess to sand the dash and vents with a 600 wet/dry paper Also I wouldn't recommend using an automotive grade paint on pleather/vinyl. They make a spray dye for that purpose. It could possibly be custom mixed to match the exterior paint. Good lookin ride!||||reg||1
Z||000003||jch82||04-09-2001||11:51 PM||||Just clean with some acetone and get some vinyl spray paint....<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||12
